        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "U5, U6, U7 — TMC2209 ... Stepper-motor drivers"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The charge-pump circuit is not wired as required, which can prevent the TMC2209 drivers from generating the gate-drive voltage needed for normal motor operation; the three dosing pumps may fail to run or operate unreliably.",
      "confidence": 0.91
    }
  ],
  "summary": "An anomaly is present: all three TMC2209 drivers have their CPO and CPI charge-pump pins bypassed to ground through separate capacitors instead of being coupled by the required charge-pump capacitor. This can compromise operation of the dosing-pump drivers."
}

